---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Vedant Nipane — Data Scientist & Writer"
  description="Portfolio of Vedant Nipane: data science, machine learning, and engineering work — plus a personal journal of poems and articles."
>
  <!-- ============ HERO ============ -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-meta">
      <span class="eyebrow status-dot"><span class="dot"></span> Data Scientist &middot; H2Loop.ai</span>
      <span class="eyebrow">Bangalore, IN</span>
    </div>

    <div class="hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-text">
        <h1 class="hero-name">Vedant<br/>Nipane<span class="accent-punct">.</span></h1>
        <p class="hero-tagline">
          Data Scientist <span class="sep">/</span>
          ML Engineer <span class="sep">/</span>
          <span class="accent-word">Occasional Writer</span>
        </p>
        <p class="hero-blurb">
          I build things with data &mdash; currently as an Associate Data
          Scientist at <strong>H2Loop.ai</strong>, working on LLM evaluation
          and dataset pipelines for domain-specific models. ECE graduate from
          <strong>IIIT Hyderabad</strong>. In the evenings I write &mdash;
          poems, essays, thoughts that don&rsquo;t fit anywhere else.
          Both feel like the same problem at 2&nbsp;AM.
        </p>

        <ul class="hero-links">
          <li><a href="mailto:vedantlnipane0@gmail.com">Email</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://linkedin.com/in/vedant-nipane-9759991b1/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://github.com/VedantNipane" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://medium.com/@lifeisgrey" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Medium</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-photo-col">
        <span class="dither-frame hero-photo">
          <img src="/profile_photo.jpg" alt="Vedant Nipane" width="220" height="220" />
        </span>
        <p class="hero-photo-caption">— portrait, 1&#8239;bit</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ ABOUT ============ -->
  <section class="block" id="about">
    <aside class="block-label">
      <span class="num">01</span>
      About
    </aside>
    <div class="block-body">
      <h2>Short version.</h2>
      <p>
        I&rsquo;m an Associate Data Scientist at <strong>H2Loop.ai</strong>,
        about a year into my career and already deep in the parts of ML I find
        most interesting &mdash; data quality, model evaluation, and the pipelines
        that make both reliable. My day-to-day spans curating large-scale technical
        datasets for domain-specific language models, designing evaluation
        frameworks to benchmark how well those models perform, and data engineering
        work that keeps it all moving. Two research preprints have come out of
        this work so far.
      </p>
      <p>
        Before H2Loop I did product analytics at <strong>Head Digital Works</strong>
        &mdash; 5.6+&nbsp;lakh game instances, cohort analysis, fraud detection.
        Before that, I was an <strong>Honours student at Remote Labs, SPCRC,
        IIIT Hyderabad</strong>, where I built <strong>Remote Titration</strong>:
        a low-cost IoT setup that lets students run real chemistry experiments
        over the web. That project got published at IEEE and won
        <strong>1st at the Hyderabad 5G-6G Hackathon</strong> and
        <strong>3rd nationally at India Mobile Congress 2024</strong>.
      </p>
      <p>
        One year in. Still learning fast. That suits me fine.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ TECH ============ -->
  <section class="block" id="tech">
    <aside class="block-label">
      <span class="num">02</span>
      Tech
    </aside>
    <div class="block-body">
      <h2>Tools of the trade.</h2>
      <dl class="tech-list">
        <div>
          <dt>Languages</dt>
          <dd>Python, SQL, C/C++</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>LLMs &amp; AI</dt>
          <dd>HuggingFace, LoRA, continual pretraining, LLM evaluation &amp; benchmarking, dataset curation</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>ML &amp; Data</dt>
          <dd>PyTorch, TensorFlow, Scikit-learn, Pandas, NumPy, MLflow, DVC</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Tools &amp; Platforms</dt>
          <dd>Docker, AWS, Git, Jupyter, PowerBI</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>DBs &amp; Frameworks</dt>
          <dd>MySQL, MongoDB, Flask, React</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ EXPERIENCE ============ -->
  <section class="block" id="experience">
    <aside class="block-label">
      <span class="num">03</span>
      Experience
    </aside>
    <div class="block-body">
      <h2>Recent work.</h2>

      <article class="job">
        <p class="meta">Sep 2025 &mdash; Present</p>
        <h3>Associate Data Scientist <span class="job-company">/ H2Loop.ai</span></h3>
        <p class="job-progression">AI Engineer Apprentice &rarr; Associate Data Scientist</p>
        <p>
          Working on quality dataset preparation for domain-specific language
          models, LLM evaluation and benchmarking pipelines, and data engineering.
          Contributed to two research preprints on traceability and continual
          pretraining for domain-specific code models.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="job">
        <p class="meta">Jun 2025 &mdash; Sep 2025</p>
        <h3>Associate Data Scientist <span class="job-company">/ Head Digital Works</span></h3>
        <p>
          Product analytics on gaming-platform redeem workflows. Analyzed 5.6+
          lakh game instances and 23+ crore in wagered amounts. Cohort analysis,
          feature strategy design, and automated fraud-detection systems.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="job">
        <p class="meta">May 2023 &mdash; May 2025</p>
        <h3>IoT Researcher <span class="job-company">/ SPCRC, IIIT Hyderabad</span></h3>
        <p>
          Led the &ldquo;Remote Titration&rdquo; project for remote lab access
          using Raspberry Pi, Python, and web tech. 1st at Hyderabad 5G-6G
          Hackathon; 3rd nationally at India Mobile Congress 2024.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ PUBLICATIONS ============ -->
  <section class="block" id="publications">
    <aside class="block-label">
      <span class="num">04</span>
      Publications
    </aside>
    <div class="block-body">
      <h2>Research &amp; writing.</h2>

      <ul class="pub-list">
        <li class="pub-item">
          <span class="pub-badge">Preprint &middot; First Author</span>
          <a class="pub-title" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.11688" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            SpecMap: Hierarchical LLM Agent for Datasheet-to-Code Traceability Link Recovery in Systems Engineering
          </a>
          <span class="pub-meta">Vedant Nipane, Pulkit Agrawal, Amit Singh &middot; arXiv 2025</span>
        </li>
        <li class="pub-item">
          <span class="pub-badge">Preprint</span>
          <a class="pub-title" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.11139" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            H2LooP Spark Preview: Continual Pretraining of Large Language Models for Low-Level Embedded Systems Code
          </a>
          <span class="pub-meta">Amit Singh, Vedant Nipane, Pulkit Agrawal et al. &middot; arXiv 2025</span>
        </li>
        <li class="pub-item">
          <span class="pub-badge">Conference Paper &middot; IEEE</span>
          <a class="pub-title" href="https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/10742986/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            Low-Cost Retrofitted IoT Based Titration Setup for Remote Labs
          </a>
          <span class="pub-meta">A. Marri, V. Nipane, R. Agrawal, S. Chaudhari, P. Bhimalapuram &middot; IEEE 2024</span>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ============ RESUMES (hidden until resume is updated) ============
  <section class="block" id="resumes">
    <aside class="block-label">
      <span class="num">05</span>
      Resume
    </aside>
    <div class="block-body">
      <h2>One resume.</h2>
      <p class="muted">Updated April 2026.</p>

      <a class="resume-card resume-card--single" href="/resumes/Vedant_Nipane_Resume.pdf" target="_blank">
        <span class="resume-kicker">PDF &middot; Apr 2026</span>
        <span class="resume-title">Vedant Nipane</span>
        <span class="resume-desc">Data Scientist &middot; ML &middot; LLM Evaluation &middot; Dataset Engineering</span>
        <span class="resume-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
  */}

  <!-- ============ JOURNAL (inverted) ============ -->
  <section class="block block--invert" id="journal">
    <aside class="block-label">
      <span class="num">06</span>
      Journal
    </aside>
    <div class="block-body">
      <h2>The quieter side.</h2>
      <p class="journal-lead">
        When the numbers are done talking, I come here to write &mdash; poems,
        essays, thoughts on life and the odd things I notice. No schedule,
        no format. Just a place to put things down.
      </p>
      <p class="journal-note">
        <span class="journal-prompt">&rarr;</span>
        <a href="/journal">Read the journal</a> &mdash;
        or find older pieces on <a href="https://medium.com/@lifeisgrey" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Medium</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ CONTACT ============ -->
  <section class="block" id="contact">
    <aside class="block-label">
      <span class="num">07</span>
      Contact
    </aside>
    <div class="block-body">
      <h2>Say hello.</h2>
      <p class="muted">Hiring, collaboration, or just to say hi.</p>
      <form class="contact-form" action="https://formspree.io/f/mqkrgqzv" method="POST">
        <div class="field-row">
          <div class="field">
            <label for="name">Name</label>
            <input id="name" name="name" type="text" required autocomplete="name" />
          </div>
          <div class="field">
            <label for="email">Email</label>
            <input id="email" name="email" type="email" required autocomplete="email" />
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="message">Message</label>
          <textarea id="message" name="message" rows="5" required></textarea>
        </div>
        <button type="submit">Send &rarr;</button>
      </form>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  /* ========= Hero ========= */
  .hero {
    padding: 2rem 0 3rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .hero-meta {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    gap: 1rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .status-dot { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; }
  .status-dot .dot {
    width: 8px; height: 8px;
    background: var(--accent);
    border-radius: 50%;
    display: inline-block;
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(164, 74, 46, 0.15);
  }

  .hero-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 240px;
    gap: 3rem;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .hero-name {
    line-height: 0.95;
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
  }
  .accent-punct {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .hero-tagline {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1.6vw, 1.25rem);
    color: var(--ink);
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
  }
  .hero-tagline .sep { color: var(--rule); margin: 0 0.35rem; }
  .accent-word {
    color: var(--accent-ink);
    font-style: italic;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .hero-blurb {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    max-width: 36em;
    margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .hero-links {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    gap: 0;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .hero-links li + li { border-left: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .hero-links a {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.7rem 1.1rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .hero-links a:hover {
    color: var(--accent-ink);
    background: var(--bg-soft);
  }

  .hero-photo-col {
    text-align: center;
  }
  .hero-photo img {
    width: 220px;
    height: 220px;
    object-fit: cover;
    filter: grayscale(1) contrast(1.15);
  }
  .hero-photo-caption {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
  }

  /* ========= Tech ========= */
  .tech-list {
    margin: 1rem 0 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .tech-list > div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    padding: 1rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .tech-list dt {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .tech-list dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }

  /* ========= Experience ========= */
  .job + .job {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .job h3 {
    margin: 0.3rem 0 0.7rem;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
  }
  .job-company {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  /* ========= Resumes ========= */
  .resume-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }
  .resume-card {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
    grid-template-rows: auto auto auto;
    gap: 0.3rem 0.5rem;
    padding: 1.25rem 1.25rem 1rem;
    background: var(--bg-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--ink);
    transition: border-color 0.15s, transform 0.15s, background 0.15s;
  }
  .resume-card:hover {
    border-color: var(--accent);
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .resume-kicker {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
  }
  .resume-title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }
  .resume-arrow {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    align-self: start;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    transition: color 0.15s, transform 0.15s;
  }
  .resume-card:hover .resume-arrow {
    color: var(--accent);
    transform: translateX(3px);
  }
  .resume-desc {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }
  .resume-card--single {
    max-width: 420px;
  }

  /* ========= Journal (inverted) ========= */
  .journal-lead {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    max-width: 36em;
  }
  .journal-note {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: #b5ad9a;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent);
    padding: 0.25rem 0 0.25rem 1rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    max-width: 40em;
  }
  .journal-prompt { color: var(--accent); margin-right: 0.35rem; }

  /* ========= Contact ========= */
  .contact-form {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    max-width: 640px;
  }
  .field-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  .field { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.3rem; }
  .field label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
  }
  .field input, .field textarea {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 1rem;
    padding: 0.65rem 0.8rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    background: #fff;
    color: var(--ink);
    border-radius: 0;
    transition: border-color 0.15s;
  }
  .field input:focus, .field textarea:focus {
    outline: none;
    border-color: var(--accent);
  }
  .contact-form button {
    align-self: flex-start;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 1rem;
    padding: 0.8rem 1.75rem;
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--ink);
    cursor: pointer;
    border-radius: 0;
    transition: background 0.15s, color 0.15s;
  }
  .contact-form button:hover {
    background: var(--accent);
    border-color: var(--accent);
  }

  /* ========= Publications ========= */
  .pub-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 1rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .pub-item {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.3rem;
    padding: 1.25rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .pub-badge {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    color: var(--accent-ink);
  }
  .pub-title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .pub-title:hover { color: var(--accent-ink); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  .pub-meta {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  /* ========= Job progression line ========= */
  .job-progression {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--accent-ink);
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
  }

  .muted { color: var(--ink-soft); }

  /* ========= Mobile ========= */
  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .hero-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 2rem;
    }
    .hero-photo-col { text-align: left; }
    .hero-photo img { width: 160px; height: 160px; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .tech-list > div {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.25rem;
      padding: 0.8rem 0;
    }
    .field-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .hero-links {
      flex-direction: column;
    }
    .hero-links li + li {
      border-left: none;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    }
  }
</style>
